        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "McDonald Property, Lucan's longest-established firm of Auctioneers, Valuers and Estate Agents, are pleased to present No. 62 Ballyowen Hall to the market.\r\n\r\nThis well-maintained first floor apartment offers a comfortable living environment within a secure gated development. Ready for immediate occupation this one bedroom apartment will appeal to a wide range of purchasers seeking a convenient and well-connected location.\r\n\r\nLocated within easy access to a wealth of local amenities, including Ballyowen Shopping Centre, Liffey Valley Shopping Centre, schools, parks, and excellent public transport links.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation centres around a bright open-plan living, dining and kitchen area, designed to maximise natural light and create a welcoming sense of space. Sliding glazed doors open onto a private balcony that has just had a new composite decking fitted. (Note: Some photographs show the old timber decking on balcony). The balcony enjoy attractive views overlooking Hermitage Park, providing an ideal outdoor space to relax and unwind.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen is both practical and well-appointed, featuring a range of fitted wall and floor cabinet, generous worktop space and tiled splashback. A spacious double bedroom with wood floor and fitted wardrobe benefits from an abundance of natural light with a sliding patio door to the balcony\r\n\r\nResidents of Ballyowen Hall enjoy access to landscaped communal gardens, secure electric-gated entry, surface and underground parking, CCTV monitoring throughout the development, an upgraded fire safety system, and a secure bike storage facility.\r\n\r\nThe location offers excellent connectivity, with immediate access to the N4 and N7 road networks. Ballyowen Park is situated directly opposite the development, providing a pleasant recreational amenity within easy walking distance.\r\n\r\nNo. 62 Ballyowen Hall presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a well-presented home in a mature and sought-after development.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway: with hot-press cupboard and wood floor.\r\n\r\nKitchen/ Dining/ Living Area: with fitted kitchen cabinets, coved ceiling, wood floor and a sliding patio door to balcony.\r\n\r\nBalcony: with a newly installed composite deck. Note: the photographs show the replaced timber deck.\r\n\r\nBedroom: a dual aspect room with fitted wardrobe, wood floor and sliding patio door to balcony.\r\n\r\nBathroom: with wood floor, WC, WHB, partially tiled walls and bathtub.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFeatures\r\n\r\nWell-presented first floor one bedroom apartment\r\n\r\nBright open-plan living, dining and kitchen area\r\n\r\nElectric heating\r\n\r\nDouble-glazed windows\r\n\r\nNewly installed composite decking on balcony\r\n\r\nPrivate balcony overlooking Hermitage Park\r\n\r\nSecure gated development\r\n\r\nUpgraded fire safety system\r\n\r\nLandscaped communal gardens\r\n\r\nSurface and underground resident parking\r\n\r\nSecure bike storage facility\r\n\r\nConvenient access to N4, N7 and local amenities\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nMeasurements provided are approximate and intended for guidance. Descriptions, photographs and floor plans are provided for illustrative and guidance purposes. Errors, omissions, inaccuracies, or mis-descriptions in these materials do not entitle any party to claims, actions, or compensation against McDonald Property or the vendor. Prospective buyers or interested parties are responsible for conducting their own due diligence, inspections, or other inquiries to verify the accuracy of the information provided. McDonald Property have not tested any appliances, apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Prospective buyers or interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items."
      },
